# Chroma library, modern Earth: NATURE MOMENTS, writer A (v25 prep, 10-21), from chroma-world/spheres/land-moments-v1.md.
# Poured into the Library 10-23. Ten good or mixed life events, each with the spec's
# five seeds (lever and opens copied from land.json) and one full cross cycle. Numbers live in land.json, not here.
# Moments: walk_clears, garden_comes_in, first_snow, cold_swim, storm_watched, good_harvest, spring_return,
# wild_animal, night_sky, foraging.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- walk_clears (cycle 1: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W)

== the walk that clears the head
tier: life event
land: walk_clears
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: joy
life: nature, health
horizon: moment
roles: friend, neighbour
earth: a long walk on the edge of town, and the head clears halfway up the hill
tribal: a long walk out past the last fire, where the hunting grounds open
magic: a long walk out of the tower's shadow, where the old wood begins
scene: {N} sets out with too much in the head and no plan but the hill. Halfway up, the wind turns, and the noise inside goes quiet one thought at a time.
scene W: {N} has walked this same loop every week this month, and the gate at the top knows the hand that opens it.
scene U: {N} keeps stopping to look at things: a fern, a crust of lichen, a track in the mud nobody could name.
scene B: From the top {N} can see the whole edge of town, and which of the fields has a sign on the gate.
scene R: The path goes the long way round, and the ridge goes straight up, and {N} is looking at the ridge.
scene G: There is a flat stone under an old thorn tree, and nobody else is on the hill.
scene tribal: {N} walks out past the last fire with nothing to carry and nowhere to be. Where the hunting grounds open, the noise of the camp falls away behind.
scene magic: {N} walks out of the tower's shadow until the bells are too faint to hear. At the edge of the old wood the air changes, and so does {N}.
- W | ask the walking group if you can come along with them every Saturday from now on | land: W | v: conformity, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 82
- U | learn the names of what grows along the hill path, with a pocket guide in hand | land: U | v: self-direction | lever: loyalty | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | walk the field you might buy one day, and talk with the farmer who owns it | land: B | v: achievement, power | lever: exit | foot: person neighbour | chance: 65
- R | leave the path and run the ridge, all the way to the top | land: R | v: stimulation, hedonism | lever: subvert | opens: trail_running | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 70
- G | sit on the flat stone until the birds forget you are there | land: G | v: universalism | lever: neglect | opens: wildlife_survey | foot: lesson stillness lets the world come back | chance: 85
- W>U | sign up for the guided walk the naturalists lead once a month | land: W | v: conformity, self-direction | lever: loyalty | foot: person mentor | chance: 78
- U>B | draw a better map of the hill routes and sell copies at the outdoor shop | land: U | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: found | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 55
- B>R | bet {friend} you can reach the top first, and the loser buys lunch | land: B | v: power, stimulation | lever: lead | foot: person friend | chance: 68
- R>G | take your shoes off and walk the last stretch barefoot through the wet grass | land: R | v: stimulation, universalism | lever: exit | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 72
- G>W | carry a bag up and bring down the litter other walkers left behind | land: G | v: universalism, conformity | lever: loyalty | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 85
works: Halfway up the hill the knot comes undone, and {N} walks home lighter than in weeks.
works: {N} comes back muddy to the knees and sleeps the whole night through.
fails: The rain comes in sideways, and {N} turns back with the same thoughts, only wetter.
fails: The head will not clear today; every step brings the same worry round again.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- garden_comes_in (cycle 2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W)

== the garden comes in all at once
tier: life event
land: garden_comes_in
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: joy
life: nature, home
horizon: moment
roles: neighbour, friend, elder
earth: the plot in late summer, when the beans and marrows come faster than anyone can eat them
tribal: the clearing by the stream in late summer, when the gourds and beans ripen all at once
magic: the walled herb garden below the tower in late summer, heavy with everything at once
scene: It is late summer, and the garden has stopped asking and started giving: beans by the bucket, marrows the size of an arm, tomatoes splitting on the vine. {N} stands in the middle of it with a basket that is already too small.
scene W: There is a list on the shed door of who on the street has had what, and {neighbour} is next.
scene U: {N} sowed three kinds of bean in three rows this spring, and one row has clearly won.
scene B: At the prices in the shops, the baskets by the gate are worth a fair bit.
scene R: There is far too much of everything, and {N} would like to eat it all tonight, with everyone.
scene G: The bees are working the last flowers, and one corner has gone to seed on its own.
scene tribal: The gourds and beans in the stream clearing have ripened all at once, more than the family can carry. {N} fills a basket, and there is still more.
scene magic: The walled garden under the tower is heavy with herbs and fruit, and the gardener has left {N} to bring it in. The baskets fill faster than the cellar can take them.
- W | leave a box of the glut on every doorstep along the street | land: W | v: benevolence, tradition | lever: loyalty | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- U | keep notes on which seeds did best, row by row, for next spring | land: U | v: self-direction, achievement | lever: loyalty | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
- B | take the surplus to the Saturday market and sell it off a trestle table | land: B | v: achievement | lever: exit | opens: market_garden | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 65
- R | throw a feast with all of it at once, and call in anyone passing | land: R | v: hedonism, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
- G | save the best seed, and let one corner run wild for the bees | land: G | v: universalism, tradition | lever: neglect | opens: beekeeping | foot: lesson a wild corner feeds the rest | chance: 85
- W>B | enter the best of it in the summer show and play by the judges' rules | land: W | v: conformity, achievement | lever: loyalty | foot: place gather.great | chance: 55
- B>G | swap your surplus with the other plot-holders for their cuttings and seedlings | land: B | v: achievement, benevolence | lever: fund | foot: person friend | chance: 78
- G>U | ask {elder} how the old growers kept beans through the winter, and write it all down | land: G | v: tradition, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: person mentor | chance: 80
- U>R | pickle, dry and ferment the lot, one wild experiment every night | land: U | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 62
- R>W | turn up at the hall kitchen with the whole harvest and cook for the lunch club | land: R | v: benevolence, stimulation | lever: lead | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 72
works: The kitchen smells of it for a week, and {N} has never felt so plainly fed by their own hands.
works: Every jar and basket finds a home, and next year's plan is already forming.
fails: Half of it spoils before anyone can eat it, and {N} composts the guilt along with the marrows.
fails: The slugs and a wet week get there first, and the glut turns out smaller than it looked.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- first_snow (cycle 1: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W)

== the first snow
tier: life event
land: first_snow
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 5-90
per_year: .33 .33 .33 .33 .33 .33
tone: joy
life: nature, leisure
horizon: moment
roles: neighbour, friend, sibling, parent
earth: the first snow of winter, fallen overnight, so the street wakes up quiet
tribal: the first snow of the cold season, falling on the camp before dawn
magic: the first snow of winter, settling on the tower roofs and the market square
scene: {N} wakes to a strange light and a deeper quiet, and the street outside has gone soft and new overnight. Nobody has walked on it yet.
scene W: {neighbour}'s path is still deep, and {neighbour} should not be out on ice.
scene U: {N} wonders how deep it is, and whether it came earlier than last year.
scene B: Half the driveways on the street are still buried, and people have places to be.
scene R: There is enough for a proper fight, and {friend} is already at the window.
scene G: Past the last houses the fields are untouched, and the only sound is the snow itself.
scene tribal: Snow fell on the camp before dawn, the first of the cold season. {N} steps out of the shelter into a world without tracks.
scene magic: The first snow lies on the tower roofs and the market square, and the lamps glow in it. Even the ravens on the battlements are quiet.
- W | take the shovel round and clear {neighbour}'s path before anyone slips | land: W | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- U | measure the depth at the gate each morning and keep a log of the whole winter | land: U | v: self-direction | lever: neglect | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 80
- B | build the biggest snowman on the street and claim the best spot | land: B | v: achievement, power | lever: voice | foot: lesson the best spot goes early | chance: 70
- R | start a snowball war that pulls in the whole street | land: R | v: stimulation, hedonism | lever: loyalty | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- G | walk out alone past the last houses, into the quiet fields | land: G | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: neglect | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 85
- W>U | follow the steps in an old library book and build a proper snow shelter | land: W | v: conformity, self-direction | lever: loyalty | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- U>B | wax the old sledge and find the fastest line down to win the race | land: U | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: lead | foot: place gather.games | chance: 60
- B>R | build the biggest snowman on the street, then dare the others to beat it | land: B | v: power, stimulation | lever: lead | foot: person rival | chance: 65
- R>G | lie in the fresh snow and sweep out shapes until the cold gets in | land: R | v: hedonism, universalism | lever: neglect | foot: means health+.02 | chance: 80
- G>W | scatter seed and put out water for the birds, and keep it up all winter | land: G | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
works: The snow holds all day, and {N} comes in glowing and soaked to the knees, happier than in weeks.
works: By evening the street is full of tracks and laughter, and {N} made half of both.
fails: By noon it has turned to grey slush, and the spell of the morning goes with it.
fails: The snow is too thin to do anything with, and {N} stands in it, waiting for more that does not come.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cold_swim (cycle 2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W)

== the cold swim
tier: life event
land: cold_swim
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: joy
life: nature, health
horizon: moment
roles: friend, neighbour
earth: a cold swim on a summer morning, in the river pool below the weir
tribal: a cold swim in the deep pool where the river bends below the camp
magic: a cold swim in the lake under the tower, where the meltwater comes down from the peaks
scene: The water is far colder than the day, and {N} stands on the edge with the breath already short. Then in, and the cold is a shout through the whole body, and then something like joy.
scene W: The morning swimmers have come here for years, and today they nod to {N} as one of them.
scene U: {N} has noticed that the water moves differently past the far bank, faster and darker.
scene B: People drive past this spot every day and have no idea it is here.
scene R: There is a high rock on the far side, and someone has scratched a tally of jumps into it.
scene G: The water is still, and the sky is in it, and {N} wants to lie in both.
scene tribal: The deep pool below the camp is cold enough to stop the breath. {N} wades in to the waist, then goes under, and comes up shouting.
scene magic: The lake under the tower is fed by meltwater from the peaks and stays cold all summer. {N} goes in from the old landing stage, and the cold rings like a bell.
- W | join the morning swimmers and help them sweep the steps afterwards | land: W | v: conformity, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 82
- U | learn how the currents run before swimming out past the shallows | land: U | v: self-direction, security | lever: neglect | opens: sailing | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 78
- B | put the swim spot on the visitors' map and charge a little to guide people | land: B | v: achievement, power | lever: voice | opens: shore_business | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 60
- R | climb the high rock and jump, feet first, into the deep part | land: R | v: stimulation | lever: subvert | opens: wild_swimming | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 65
- G | float face up and let the water take the weight, eyes on the sky | land: G | v: universalism, hedonism | lever: neglect | foot: lesson the water holds you up | chance: 85
- W>B | train to the club's timetable to win the summer race across the lake | land: W | v: conformity, achievement | lever: loyalty | foot: place gather.games | chance: 55
- B>G | talk the landowner into leaving the gate to the pool open for everyone | land: B | v: power, universalism | lever: voice | foot: person neighbour | chance: 55
- G>U | ask the old swimmer who has come here forty years what the water does each month | land: G | v: tradition, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- U>R | read the current, then try the long swim across the pool to the far bank | land: U | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: subvert | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 62
- R>W | dare {friend} and the whole crowd in, then keep them coming back every week | land: R | v: stimulation, benevolence | lever: found | foot: person friend | chance: 70
works: {N} comes out shaking and laughing, and the cold glow lasts until lunchtime.
works: The whole day after feels clean and sharp at the edges, and {N} sleeps like a stone.
fails: The cold wins inside a minute, and {N} is out again, gasping, with nothing to show but chattering teeth.
fails: The water is murkier than it looked, and {N} climbs out feeling worse than before.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- storm_watched (cycle 1: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W)

== the storm from the window
tier: life event
land: storm_watched
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: mixed
life: nature, home
horizon: moment
roles: neighbour, partner, parent, friend
earth: a big storm, watched from the kitchen window while the lights flicker
tribal: a big storm over the plain, watched from the mouth of the cave
magic: a great storm over the valley, watched from a high window of the tower
scene: The storm comes in at dusk, and {N} watches it from behind the glass: trees bent flat, rain in sheets, the street lamps shaking. Somewhere a gate bangs and bangs.
scene W: {neighbour} lives alone, and {Ns} eyes keep going to their dark window.
scene U: The forecast said it would peak at nine, and {N} has the clock and the barometer side by side.
scene B: An old tree in the lane is coming down, and that is a lot of good timber.
scene R: Every gust pulls at {N} like a hand on the sleeve: come out.
scene G: The roar has a rhythm to it, if {N} listens long enough.
scene tribal: The storm crosses the plain like a running herd, and the clan watches it from the mouth of the cave. {N} sits nearest the edge, where the spray reaches.
scene magic: From a high window of the tower {N} watches the storm walk down the valley, lightning in its hands. The old glass hums with every gust.
- W | go round the neighbours when it eases, door by door, to see who needs a hand | land: W | v: benevolence, security | lever: loyalty | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- U | track it hour by hour, and check it against the forecast in the morning | land: U | v: self-direction | lever: neglect | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 78
- B | head out at first light to gather the fallen branches before anyone else does | land: B | v: achievement, security | lever: exit | opens: wood_crafts | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 70
- R | step out into the storm and let it hit you full in the face | land: R | v: stimulation | lever: subvert | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- G | lie awake and listen to it all night, without trying to sleep | land: G | v: universalism | lever: neglect | foot: lesson fear and wonder sit together | chance: 85
- W>U | note which drains overflow and send the list to the council in the morning | land: W | v: security, self-direction | lever: voice | opens: flood_warden | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- U>B | catch the lightning on a long exposure and enter the best shot in a competition | land: U | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: lead | foot: place arts.craft | chance: 50
- B>R | bet {friend} on how many trees come down by morning, then go out early to count | land: B | v: power, stimulation | lever: subvert | foot: person friend | chance: 60
- R>G | open every window and let the wind and the smell of rain through the house | land: R | v: stimulation, universalism | lever: neglect | foot: lesson a house can take some weather | chance: 72
- G>W | light candles, make tea, and keep everyone in the house together till it passes | land: G | v: benevolence, tradition | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
works: When it is over the air is washed and strange, and for a moment {N} feels the size of the world.
works: The house holds, and in the morning the street comes out to look at it all together.
fails: The storm takes the fence and half the night's sleep, and {N} spends the next day tired and on edge.
fails: A branch comes through the shed roof, and the wonder of it is gone by morning.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- good_harvest (cycle 2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W)

== the good harvest
tier: life event
land: good_harvest
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .2 .2 .2 .2 .2
tone: joy
life: nature, work
horizon: moment
roles: parent, neighbour, sibling, friend
earth: a good year on the farm: the barns full and the price holding
tribal: a good year on the river flats: the grain stores full and the herds fat
magic: a good year on the tower's farms: the granaries full and the steward smiling
scene: It has been a good year: the rain came when it should and stopped when it should, and the barns are full to the doors. {parent} stands in the yard, doing sums in the head and smiling at them.
scene W: There is a harvest supper in the village hall every year, and the first share has always gone to it.
scene U: The low field floods in every wet year, and this year there is money to fix it.
scene B: The field next door has been for sale since spring, and now there is enough.
scene R: After a year like this, {N} wants one night in town that nobody forgets.
scene G: The birds have followed the harvester all week, and the hedges are loud with them.
scene tribal: The grain stores on the river flats are full, and the herds are fat for the cold. The clan gathers to decide what the good year is for.
scene magic: The tower's granaries are full to the rafters, and the steward has left a purse on the table. {N} has a say in where it goes.
