# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wild_animal (cycle 2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W)

== the wild thing on the path
tier: life event
land: wild_animal
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 5-90
per_year: .25 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: joy
life: nature, leisure
horizon: moment
roles: friend, parent, sibling, elder
earth: a fox, a deer, a heron or an owl crossing the path at dusk on the edge of town
tribal: a fox, an elk, a heron or an owl crossing the path at dusk beyond the camp
magic: a fox, a stag, a heron or an owl crossing the path at dusk, with eyes that seem to know you
scene: At dusk, on the edge of town, something wild steps onto the path ahead: a fox, or a deer, or a heron lifting off the ditch. It stops and looks at {N}, and for a moment neither of them moves.
scene W: {N} has heard that the town keeps a count of its wild animals, and this one should be on it.
scene U: It is a long way from where its kind should be, and {N} wonders why.
scene B: {N} has the camera ready, and the light is perfect.
scene R: It turns and slips into the hedge, and {N} wants to go after it.
scene G: It has not run yet. If {N} stays perfectly still, it might not.
scene tribal: At dusk, beyond the last fire, an elk steps out of the trees and stands in the path. The clan has stories about such meetings, and {N} remembers all of them at once.
scene magic: An owl lands on the gatepost at dusk and turns its head to look at {N}, slow and certain. The old ones say such creatures carry messages, if anyone stays still enough to hear.
