- R | follow it into the hedge and along the ditch, as far as it goes | land: R | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: exit | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 60
- G | stay perfectly still and let it go on its way | land: G | v: universalism | lever: neglect | foot: lesson the wild does not need us | chance: 88
- W>B | write it up for the town newsletter, with your own name under it | land: W | v: conformity, achievement | lever: voice | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 65
- B>G | ask the landowner to leave its hedge uncut, and promise to keep watch | land: B | v: power, universalism | lever: voice | foot: door kept your word | chance: 55
- G>U | ask {elder} what the old folk said it means when one crosses your path | land: G | v: tradition, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- U>R | sit up at the window with a torch and notebook to see if it returns | land: U | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 60
