# ---------------------------------------------------------------- foraging (cycle 2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W)

== the autumn hedges
tier: life event
land: foraging
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: joy
life: nature, friends
horizon: moment
roles: friend, grandparent, neighbour
earth: an autumn afternoon along the hedges and the edge of the wood, with a basket
tribal: an autumn afternoon in the hazel thickets, gathering for the cold months
magic: an autumn afternoon in the old wood below the tower, where the herb-wives gather
scene: Autumn, and the hedges are heavy with it: sloes, rosehips, hazelnuts, the last brambles, mushrooms pushing up through the leaves. {N} has a basket and an afternoon and nobody waiting.
scene W: {grandparent} always said it: never more than a third, and leave the rest for the birds and the next one along.
scene U: There is a cluster of mushrooms at the foot of the oak, and {N} is nearly sure what they are. Nearly.
scene B: The new restaurant in town pays well for wild things, and {N} knows where the best ones grow.
scene R: There is one bush loaded with fruit, and nobody else has found it yet.
scene G: {N} only needs enough for tonight, and the hedge has more than enough.
scene tribal: The hazel thickets are full, and the band has gone out to gather for the cold months. {N} knows the old rule, and knows the best tree.
scene magic: The herb-wives gather in the old wood below the tower each autumn, and this year {N} goes with a basket of their own. The wood is generous, and watching.
- W | pick by the old rule, never more than a third of any bush | land: W | v: tradition, conformity | lever: loyalty | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 85
